\title{fastRhockey: Access Hockey Play-by-Play Data and Statistics}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Scrape and load hockey play-by-play data and statistics. Sources include the National Hockey League (NHL) \url{https://www.nhl.com/} web, stats, 'NHL Edge' tracking and records application programming interfaces (APIs), the Professional Women's Hockey League \url{https://www.thepwhl.com/}, and the American Hockey League, Ontario Hockey League, Western Hockey League and Quebec Maritimes Junior Hockey League through their 'HockeyTech' feeds. It also reads NHL data from 'ESPN' and 'Fox Sports', National Collegiate Athletic Association (NCAA) men's and women's hockey from 'ESPN', and 13 European leagues: Germany's Deutsche Eishockey Liga (DEL), Austria's International Central European (ICE) Hockey League, the United Kingdom's Elite Ice Hockey League (EIHL), Denmark's Metal Ligaen, the Kontinental Hockey League (KHL), Russia's Supreme Hockey League (VHL), the Swedish Hockey League (SHL) and HockeyAllsvenskan, Finland's Liiga, Switzerland's National League and Swiss Ice Hockey Federation competitions, Czechia's Extraliga and France's Ligue Magnus. Loaders read pre-scraped play-by-play, box score, schedule and expected-goals datasets from the 'SportsDataverse' data releases.
}
\section{Proxy support}{

All HTTP requests flow through an internal httr2 helper that resolves a proxy
in this order:
\enumerate{
\item an explicit \verb{proxy =} argument (only on wrappers that pass \code{...});
\item \code{getOption("fastRhockey.proxy")} -- set once per session with
\code{options(fastRhockey.proxy = "http://host:port")} and every call
picks it up;
\item the \code{http_proxy} / \code{https_proxy} / \code{no_proxy} environment variables,
read by libcurl when no explicit proxy is supplied.
}
The proxy value may be a URL string (\code{"http://host:port"}) or a named list
spread into \code{\link[httr2:req_proxy]{httr2::req_proxy()}} for authenticated proxies, e.g.
\code{list(url = "http://host", port = 8080, username = "u", password = "p", auth = "basic")}. The session-\code{options()} form is recommended when one proxy
covers many calls.
}

